<title>SWEDEN: Astra posts one pct rise in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Astra posts one pct rise in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs group Astra reports its earnings for the three months ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    3,455 vs  3,437</p>
<p> Sales					10,133 vs  9,337</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 4.04 vs  3.99</p>
<p> Operating costs			   6,771 vs  6,158</p>
<p> Operating profit			  3,362 vs  3,179</p>
<p> Net financial items		 CREDIT 92 vs    257 CREDIT</p>
<p> Minorities			     CREDIT 1 vs	1 CREDIT</p>
<p> Tax					     965 vs    976</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,490 vs  2,461</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found analysts were expecting a pre-tax profit of 3.93 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
